Hey YouTubers, this is Charlie

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.596
This is going to be my walking dead Episode 15 video.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.940
subheading - Crazy Rick episode

00:00:07.945 --> 00:00:09.915
There is so much awesome stuff to get to, so I'll just 

00:00:09.915 --> 00:00:12.276
- just remind everyone that a new round of the giveaway

00:00:12.276 --> 00:00:12.776
starts now.

00:00:12.776 --> 00:00:14.148
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber

00:00:14.148 --> 00:00:15.915
and leave a comment on this video

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:18.815
Careful for  spoilers if you haven't seen the episode yet.

00:00:18.815 --> 00:00:20.240
Starting with my top 5 moments

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.360
#5 is Nine Inch Walking Dead Nails

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.140
Technically, the band is broken up -

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.920
but I love the mix that Deanna's family was listening to

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.735
- such a great way to open the episode 

00:00:30.735 --> 00:00:33.420
I think I've mentioned it in previous episodes before but the Walking Dead

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.098
- tries to mix things up with the ways they shoot their intros.

00:00:36.098 --> 00:00:38.094
Like, sometimes they'll be really cinematic...

00:00:38.094 --> 00:00:40.054
Sometimes they'll use really interesting music...

00:00:40.054 --> 00:00:42.908
I think my second favorite music episode of The Walking Dead

00:00:42.908 --> 00:00:46.780
 -- or music intro was the Bob intro from Season 4

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.110
Both very sad ways to open the episode

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.953
but I felt like the Bob one was a little more melancholy 

00:00:51.953 --> 00:00:54.678
The Trent Reznor music is just to get you Amped Up

00:00:54.678 --> 00:00:56.954
which is why they intercut with Carols oven heating up

00:00:57.095 --> 00:00:59.495
The oven of Alexandria is heating up

00:00:59.495 --> 00:01:01.940
They also had the Carl and Enid kitchen timer thing too

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.960
I just love the way cooking is a metaphor in the finale

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.394
Even though Deanna seems super pissed

00:01:06.394 --> 00:01:08.674
that she left the casserole on the door step

00:01:08.674 --> 00:01:11.934
It still feels like she's coming from a place of sanity

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:13.187
like, she hasn't completely lost it yet

00:01:13.187 --> 00:01:15.515
She's a politician so - she knows how it goes

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:19.380
On to #4 Deanna and Rick argue about what to do with Pete.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.075
This is a really good example of balancing forces in the episode

00:01:22.075 --> 00:01:25.694
so, like, they don't want you to think that any one character

00:01:25.694 --> 00:01:27.428
...is more right than the other.

00:01:27.428 --> 00:01:29.176
Rick's perspective is valid

00:01:29.214 --> 00:01:30.494
and Deanna's is too

00:01:30.494 --> 00:01:32.119
She doesn't want to kill anyone but - 

00:01:32.119 --> 00:01:34.555
Rick doesn't want to let the abuse continue.

00:01:34.555 --> 00:01:37.050
Really the thing that sells it for me is when Rick -

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:40.697
- tells Jesse later that inside here is the same as out there.

00:01:40.697 --> 00:01:43.354
it depends on whether or not you believe him when he says that.

00:01:43.354 --> 00:01:45.114
and which side you come down on.

00:01:45.114 --> 00:01:48.114
- if you agree that the rules of the outside world should..

00:01:48.135 --> 00:01:51.175
..be the same as the rules inside Alexandria.

00:01:51.175 --> 00:01:52.763
if so, then you're in Ricks camp.

00:01:52.763 --> 00:01:55.095
I think that most people will come down on Ricks side.

00:01:55.095 --> 00:01:58.360
Letting wounds fester, like Pete being a giant wound

00:01:58.495 --> 00:02:01.855
will only cause Alexandria to rot from the inside.

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:04.375
its not going to get better, people will still die no matter what.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:08.100
whether they die by abuse or Rick's Revolver

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.740
On to #3, Sasha goes Crazy.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:16.160
I don't mean literally crazy, but that she's going a little nuts all over walkers.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.160
Michonne and Rosita went a little nuts too

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:21.665
I think they took the opportunity to let off some steam in the woods.

00:02:21.665 --> 00:02:23.574
They want you to think sasha's going nuts-

00:02:23.574 --> 00:02:26.374
- but really, she hasn't done anything that doesn't need to be done.

00:02:26.374 --> 00:02:29.600
someone needs to take care of all the walkers, so why not her.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.155
She's actually doing them a service.

00:02:31.155 --> 00:02:34.579
And even though she took down Rick at the end of the episode 

00:02:34.579 --> 00:02:37.695
I still think Michonne is going back and forth about the way she wants to live her life.

00:02:38.486 --> 00:02:44.086
Like, if she wants to adopt the Alexandria way of life or be the person with the katana

00:02:44.086 --> 00:02:49.357
I love that flashback scene. That was the first time in Season one that she appeared.

00:02:49.357 --> 00:02:51.600
Or technically that was the season 2 finale.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:58.175
That's the mode that Sasha is in right now and I feel like Michonne is going to take her katanna off the wall in the finale at some point.

00:02:58.175 --> 00:03:01.500
Something really important to remember too, Sasha is hanging up in the tower.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:05.014
She kinda saw there was a commotion going on with Rick's fight at the end but

00:03:05.014 --> 00:03:08.032
she used the opportunity to pick off a bunch of walkers at the wall

00:03:08.032 --> 00:03:12.520
Nicholas, the one that had stolen Rick's gun and hidden it in a coffee can - stole it

00:03:13.175 --> 00:03:20.175
he heard the gunshots at the wall. They didn't address that, but I'm wondering if Nicholas is going to overlap with Sasha in the tower.

00:03:20.175 --> 00:03:23.734
If anyone were going to be the one to take him down, I would want Sasha to be the one to do it.

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:27.814
Moving on to #2. Daryl and Aaron find more signs of the Wolves.

00:03:27.814 --> 00:03:32.817
They waited until the end of the episode to explain it, but they've been finding dead walkers all over the place.

00:03:32.817 --> 00:03:37.782
Then they found the ones chopped up into bits, then they found the one tied to the tree.

00:03:37.782 --> 00:03:42.774
And if it wasn't entirely clear when they said it, she was alive when they tied her to the tree.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:46.660
meaning that these "Wolves" are sick as shit

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:52.430
If you remember the episode where Tyreese died, there was a sign that read "Wolves not far"

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:57.775
I've said it in previous episodes, but I think that the Wolves are stand ins for the scavengers from the comics.

00:03:57.775 --> 00:04:04.113
Just a terrible group in the DC area...not to be confused with Negan and the Saviours. Totally different group.

00:04:04.113 --> 00:04:09.433
That doesn't answer the question of where Morgan is. I know that a whole bunch of people were hoping Daryl would run into Morgan.

00:04:09.433 --> 00:04:13.280
he could still show up in the finale. There are still a whole bunch of question about Morgans storyline and how 

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:16.900
it's going to tie back in with the survivors

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.160
So just open up a bookmark in Google Chrome for Wolves and Morgan

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:24.040
And my number one moment, RICK vs. PORCHDICK

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:28.375
I think we were all expecting this to happens so I don't think this is a surprise. It's from the comics

00:04:28.375 --> 00:04:32.655
I think the way that they're doing it on the show is just a little bit more drawn out.

00:04:32.655 --> 00:04:39.394
But I think its going the way we all expected. Alexandria is Thunder Dome. Two Men Enter, One Man Leaves

00:04:39.394 --> 00:04:45.517
All I could think about during the fight was Peter Griffin vs the giant chicken on family guy.

00:04:45.517 --> 00:04:52.295
In all seriousness though, they wanted you to question who would win the fight - like - they didn't want it to be a easy win for Rick

00:04:52.475 --> 00:04:57.035
He's a big guy and it's gonna take a lot to take him down with his fists.

00:04:57.035 --> 00:05:03.114
Normally he'd just shoot him but because he is in that community, Rick was hesitant to draw his gun and fire.

00:05:03.114 --> 00:05:08.280
That scene right after he talked to Jesse the first time was him just looking at all the kids and people sitting around

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:12.900
You'd think that he was formulating a plan but honestly I don't think he has much of a plan in his head

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:16.355
He's just like I'm gonna deal with this the way I deal with everything

00:05:16.355 --> 00:05:23.315
The problem is that they're in Alexandria and there is a giant group of people living there and people aren't used to his way of doing things.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:31.700
It was so much fun watching Rick try to explain himself to Jesse - hes so inarticulate, he couldn't come out and say I really care about you

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:35.640
That's his neanderthal way of telling her that he really cares about her

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:41.860
Love in the time of the apocalypse. I haven't heard anything about Jesse surviving to season 6. Hopefully she makes it 

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:47.460
I would like to see something happen between them, but first, porch dick has to be removed from the equation.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:52.693
So here is my question for you guys. How do you think they are going to resolve the Rick vs Porch Dick situation.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:06:01.440
It seems like what they are suggesting is that Rick will end up killing Pete but somehow the Wolves storyline will intersect with that

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:07.980
So it wont just be Rick vs Pete. It will be Rick vs Pete in this greater context of the Wolves

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:14.500
And a giant army of walkers that seems to be massing at the gates more and more. It's kinda of like the prison round 2.

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:16.972
Only this time, Ricks group is the invading force.

00:06:16.972 --> 00:06:23.372
I've seen a lot of comments from you guys asking if Rick is the villain this time around

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:30.140
Has he turned into Shane or has he turned into the Governor. I don't this that he has but anybody who has

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:37.040
stumbled upon this episode without knowing who Rick was, and watched that scene at the end, they would thing Rick is crazy

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.840
like oh my god, what is wrong with this guy.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:42.320
It isn't untill you have the broader context that you start to sympathize with Rick more.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:45.520
because look at all the things he's been through

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:49.695
because if they head dealt with the governor the same way, then woodbury probably wouldn't have gone down the same way.

00:06:49.695 --> 00:06:52.594
People probably wouldn't have died. Same thing goes for the prison.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:07:00.880
If you want to think about the Rick and Shane comparison think about it like this. Shane was much quicker to sacrifice members of the group.

00:07:00.883 --> 00:07:04.580
I think Rick still thinks about it like it's still a measure of last resort.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:09.120
but he wont hesitate when he decides that somebody need to "go"

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:13.720
They've changed a few things from the comics. If you've read them, just use spoiler tags.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:17.880
It's a little more clear cut in the comic which decision has to be made - like - what Rick has to do

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:22.760
In the circumstances in the show that are keeping Pete alive aren't quite the same in the comics.

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:25.940
He's not quite as necessary to the people of Alexandria as he is in the show.

